# The paths specy-road writes at run time are ignored by the managed block
# below, which `specy-road init project` writes and `specy-road refresh-stubs`
# keeps current. Add your own rules outside the block; the block is rewritten.
# The comments here explain what the block ignores, and what it deliberately
# leaves tracked.
#
# Session-scoped work artifacts created by specy-road do-next-available-task
# (work/.on-complete-*.yaml, work/prompt-*.md, work/.milestone-session.yaml).
# These are regenerated each pickup; tracking them adds noise to feature
# branches. Briefs (work/brief-*.md) and implementation summaries
# (work/implementation-summary-*.md) are intentionally NOT ignored — they
# document the work and belong on the feature branch.
#
# work/pr-body-*.md is the finish-this-task snapshot passed to
# `gh pr create --body-file`. It is a concatenation of the brief and the
# implementation summary, so tracking it duplicates both in git history.
#
# work/brainstorm-*-prompt.md is regenerated by `specy-road brainstorm start`
# and `recommend` from the session plus the current graph. The session itself
# (work/brainstorm-*.yaml) is NOT ignored: the ideas that were rejected are as
# much a record of the reasoning as the ones that became roadmap nodes.
#
# Review hand-offs (work/reviews/: READY-*, REVIEW-*, PACKET.md; see
# docs/orchestration.md). A review binds to the commit it read, so committing
# the review would move the branch past that commit. The approving reviews are
# recorded as Reviewed-by trailers on the mark-implementation-reviewed commit
# instead.
# Agent presence records (work/.sessions/, specy-road session); per checkout,
# never shared via git.
# Worker records, event logs and linked worktrees (work/.workers/,
# work/.worktrees/; specy-road worker).
#
# Derived indexes for `specy-road history` and `specy-road search`
# (.specyrd/cache/). Rebuilt from git and the working tree on demand, so they
# are never committed; .specyrd/manifest.json stays tracked.
#
# roadmap.md and roadmap-context.md are deliberately absent from this file.
# Both are generated, and both are COMMITTED: `roadmap.md` is the human index
# and `roadmap-context.md` (specy-road digest) is what an agent reads instead of
# crawling planning/ and work/. Regenerate them when the graph changes; gate CI
# on `specy-road export --check` and `specy-road digest --check`.
#
# Per-checkout capacity pauses (available / paused_until) without pushing the
# shared roster; merged at runtime with roadmap/orchestration.yaml. The ignore
# rule lives in agent_ignores.GITIGNORE_LINES (managed block below).
